cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Before the Backtest: Pre-Freeze Common-Support Ceilings for Event-Driven Strategy Research"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
abstract: >-
  A pre-freeze common-support ceiling: a procedure that computes the maximum attainable matched
  support on the complete point-in-time eligible population, before a matched event-study design is
  frozen and before any outcome column is opened, and stops the study if the implied confirmatory
  sample falls below a pre-registered minimum. Demonstrated on 62 candidate cryptocurrency delisting
  events, where the implied confirmatory sample is 10 against a required 40 and no price column was
  ever loaded.
authors:
  - family-names: "Ramos Silva"
    given-names: "Ricardo H."
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-13"
keywords:
  - common support
  - positivity
  - outcome-free design
  - point-in-time data
  - event studies
  - pre-registration
  - research feasibility
